# test.manifest: the automated end-to-end test image.
#
# The freestanding syscall probes (build/tests) at the root, the musl integration
# programs (build/tests/musl) under /musl, a minimal /etc the musl file and auth
# probes read, and the small name-resolution config the network probes read.
# `make test` boots this image and asserts every probe's success token. Host
# paths are relative to the repo root (mkimage.sh cd's there).

exec-dir 0755 / build/tests

# suidprobe's fixtures: the same helper binary staged at several modes and
# owners. exec-dir above already placed a plain 0755 /suidhelper (the "plain"
# control); these add the setuid-root copy suidprobe execs to gain root, a
# setuid copy owned by a non-root uid (the bit grants that owner's identity), a
# setgid copy owned by a non-root group, and a setuid-but-no-x copy the execute
# check must still refuse. Explicit modes and owners override the exec-dir
# default for these paths.
file 04755:0:0 /suidhelper.suid build/tests/suidhelper
file 04755:5:0 /suidhelper.u5   build/tests/suidhelper
file 02755:0:5 /suidhelper.sgid build/tests/suidhelper
file 04644:0:0 /suidhelper.nox  build/tests/suidhelper

# sudoprobe's fixtures: the reference sudo (utils/sudo.c, the coursework answer
# key) staged setuid root, and a sudoers listing uid 1000. sudoprobe drops to
# 1000, runs sudo to become root, and to 1001 to be refused. Shipped only here;
# neither shipped image carries a sudo, deliberately, since writing one is the
# exercise this fixture is the answer key to.
file 04755:0:0 /sudo build/utils/sbin/sudo
text 0644 /etc/sudoers # uids permitted to run sudo\n1000\n

# pwauthmusl's target: the setuid-root su (utils/su.c), the same binary and the
# same mode os-simple carries, so the probe drives what a user runs rather than
# a copy of it. The probe's own account is `probe` below, whose
# shell is the /idreport helper the exec-dir sweep already staged, so a su run
# reports the identity, the working directory, the argv[0] and the environment
# it was given and exits non-zero on the first item that does not match.
file 04755:0:0 /su build/utils/sbin/su
file 04755:0:0 /passwd build/utils/sbin/passwd
file 0755:0:0 /adduser build/utils/sbin/adduser
file 0755:0:0 /adduser-crash build/utils/sbin/adduser-crash
file 0755:0:0 /login build/utils/sbin/login

# The probe account's home. It is a real directory and not the image root,
# because a chdir to the directory the caller is already in would prove nothing
# about what a login su does; the probe runs su from /musl and requires the
# login form to land here and the non-login form not to. 0700 owned by the
# account, so entering it is the target's privilege and not the caller's.
dir 0755 /home
dir 0700:1000:1000 /home/probe

# searchprobe's fixtures: a root-owned tree whose modes the probe flips to prove
# search is charged on every directory a path enters. Staged rather than minted
# because the execve cases need a real program under the denied ancestor and a
# freestanding probe cannot mint an ELF; the directories that hold it come with
# it, and the probe asserts these modes before it flips anything. Everything the
# probe's mutations aim at it mints and removes itself, so this tree is what it
# finds on every run. Every directory here is 0777, because the probe denies by
# turning one of them into 0666: read and write stay granted, so only the
# missing execute bit can account for a refusal. /sp_denied/shared keeps its
# 0777 while /sp_denied is denied, so a refusal below it can only be the
# ancestor's search bit.
dir  0777 /sp_denied
dir  0777 /sp_denied/deep
dir  0777 /sp_denied/shared
text 0644 /sp_denied/leaf.txt one level down\n
text 0644 /sp_denied/deep/leaf.txt two levels down\n
file 0755 /sp_denied/prog build/tests/hello

# stickyprobe's pair: one sticky directory and one plain one, differing in the
# single bit whose enforcement the probe tests, so that a denial in the first
# cannot be ownership or a missing write bit talking. They are staged rather
# than minted for the one reason minting cannot cover: `dir 1777` is how the
# shipped /tmp gets its bit, and nothing else in the tree reads that bit back,
# so the probe asserts both of these modes before it does anything. Everything
# the probe's cases aim at, and the two further sticky directories the
# directory-owner and write-check clauses need, it mints and removes itself.
dir 1777 /st_sticky
dir 0777 /st_plain

dir 0755 /musl
exec-dir 0755 /musl build/tests/musl
# suidmusl's setuid-root copy: the plain 0755 /musl/suidmusl above is the
# parent that drops to 1000 and execs this to prove libc's view of a set-id
# exec (getresuid, getauxval(AT_SECURE), the saved-id dance).
file 04755:0:0 /musl/suidmusl.suid build/tests/musl/suidmusl

# A minimal /etc: catfile reads motd and lists the directory, permmusl opens
# motd, and authmusl resolves root through passwd to uid 0. Both shadow lines
# are fixed, committed test credentials, not secrets: the probes need a known
# hash to verify against. Root's password is "rach2" and the probe account's is
# "probepass", two different ones on purpose, so offering root's to `su probe`
# is a wrong password rather than a lucky one. The probe account is uid 1000
# with /idreport as its shell and /home/probe as its home; /etc/group gives it
# the group its gid names.
dir 0755 /etc
text 0644 /etc/motd Welcome to Rach2 (test image).\n
text 0644 /etc/hostname rach2\n
text 0644 /etc/passwd root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/sh\nprobe:x:1000:1000:probe:/home/probe:/idreport\nprobe2:x:1001:1001:probe2:/home/probe:/idreport\n
text 0644 /etc/group root:x:0:\nprobe:x:1000:\nprobe2:x:1001:\n
text 0600 /etc/shadow root:$6$rach2test$br2Wb86wTtgiPWLN2WQoPqu69kGMNLnIQj3eaZLhG6sNTm9sN6ny.2af9tuaB/2HTw86.N3ZZN585IBoPgi0w/:0:0:99999:7:::\nprobe:$6$probetest$81REycl6dLv1SAkzSsuY0bx0yRoiYWOLkNshDgfNYybAChA02pRRKRGRlPADOnGg9SwQRz80cXN875vlU6LSF0:0:0:99999:7:::\nprobe2:$6$probe2test$v9NhhsuiXi4hOCF74Pbx1Wf6OFlAxvxA6U9pcCazHvodWv3lCg2LoShwjBUpyOazABVMnpgK2Ln2zNuIx2vpd0:0:0:99999:7:::\n

text 0644 /hello.txt hello, world\n
text 0644 /resolv.conf nameserver 10.0.2.3\n
text 0644 /hosts 127.0.0.1   localhost\n10.0.2.2    gateway\n10.0.2.3    dns\n10.0.2.15   rach2\n
